<title>RUSSIA: Russia 448-day bond tranche priced at 98.10 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia 448-day bond tranche priced at 98.10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new tranche of Russian 448-day OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24010) was priced at an average 98.10 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the price would be in a 97.91-98.25 percent range.</p>
<p>On Tuesday the original issue closed at 97.94, to yield 43.10 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number			24010</p>
<p>    Issue volume			 5.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		     3.76 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)		     2.00 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds			     2.16 trln</p>
<p>    Average price			98.10 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	    97.91 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield			42.45 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	   43.29 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor				  448 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date			June 17, 1998</p>
<p>    Next coupon date		   June 18, 1997</p>
<p>    Next coupon amount		 187,884 rbls</p>
<p>On Wednesday the Finance Ministry raised 4.34 trillion roubles by selling 252-day GKO discount Treasury bills making total proceeds from auctions for the day 6.50 trillion roubles.</p>
<p>It has also repaid about 6.34 trillion roubles in maturing 217-day T-bills (series 22046).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
